text:
sahil: onboarding run flagged a rerank failure - one vector in a batch was length 1535 vs expected 1536. intermittent under auth rotation.
maya: can you paste the API reject?
sahil: server log snippet: 
```
[2026-08-02T10:18:31Z] ERROR embeddings.service: reject vector_dim_mismatch expected=1536 got=1535 batch=onboard-99
```
otto: i've traced similar failures: when a token refresh triggers the retry path, our chunking logic can split a batch and the requeue step drops the last float for that item (off-by-one in tail copy).
maya: python sampleapp currently auto-pads short vectors which hides the problem for users. that's confusing during onboarding. we should be explicit.
sahil: short-term mitigation: add a pre-send validator in SDKs and samples that fails fast with clear metadata and avoid re-enqueueing the same item on auth retry.
otto: propose sdk parity change: add `strictShape=true` (default) in the embeddings/rerank helpers. when true, return 400 with machine-readable fields {error:"vector_dim_mismatch", expected, got, index, sample_id}. when false, pad/trim but emit a warning & metric.
maya: also let's make the sample CLI opt-in for padding: `--pad-on-mismatch` default false. onboarders see the real error unless they explicitly enable legacy padding.
sahil: small validator snippet (TS) i used locally: 
```ts
export function checkShapes(vecs: number[][], expected: number) {
  for (let i = 0; i < vecs.length; i++) {
    const v = vecs[i];
    if (!Array.isArray(v) || v.length !== expected) {
      return {ok: false, index: i.toString(), got: (Array.isArray(v) ? v.length.toString() : 'non-array')};
    }
  }
  return {ok: true};
}
```
maya: will update sample README to show how to opt into padding and how SDKs surface the error message.
otto: i'll patch the batching helper to fix the slice math and add a unit test that forces token expiry mid-batch (auth-refresh simulation). that should prevent regressions.
sahil: can we also emit a telemetry metric `sdk.embed.invalid_dim` with tag `sample_app=true|false` so support can surface onboarding spikes?
otto: yes, adding the metric and a short dashboard. also adding an alert if rate > X/min during ramp.
devex-bot: New issue created: DE-1830 "embeddings: strictShape default + fix auth-requeue off-by-one" (https://git.internal/redwood/issues/DE-1830) :robot_face: 
maya: thanks. i'll coordinate docs + sample PR and keep onboarding team updated. closing loop when CI canary passes and docs merge.
